			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				751,
				2
			],
			"Message": "style(Output): Standardize indentation in build scripts to 1 tab\n\nReformat `Source/Run.sh` and `Source/prepublishOnly.sh` to use consistent single-tab indentation for all shell script blocks and comments. Align the `case` statement bodies and `exit` handlers to match the project's PascalCase and indentation standards.\n\nThis change addresses the whitespace drift in the shell script helpers without altering any logic, build paths, or dependency resolution strategies. The scripts continue to correctly select `out` for Microsoft/VSCode and `Source` for CodeEditorLand/Editor dependencies.",
			"SHA": "90769b8b8889e898150a7277ad5f3ba1a94188b1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T01:02:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				751,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Standardize Tiers IPC environment variable resolution\n\nUpdate the `_TierIPC` constant initialization in `Tauri.Main.Process.Service` to use a consistent and robust fallback pattern for accessing tier configuration. Replace the previous mixed check involving `__LAND_TIERS__` with a direct safe navigation lookup on `globalThis.__LandTiers`.\n\nThis change aligns with the dual-track IPC architecture established in recent commits, ensuring the environment variable resolution logic is unified across the Output layer and reduces dependency on build-time global constants that may vary between build configurations.",
			"SHA": "29861cb62aa54fef542a14b6edfe634d1ec5d28e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T00:55:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				751,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Route polyfill diagnostics through Mountain IPC and suppress errors\n\nIn `Disable/Lazy/Paint.ts`, removed direct `console.error` calls in polyfill callbacks. Replaced with silent error swallowing to prevent stack traces for non-fatal lifecycle errors.\n\nIn `Telemetry/Consent/Off.ts`, replaced direct `console.log` with a conditional `MountainIPCInvoke` call targeting `diagnostic:log`. This aligns the telemetry notification with the unified diagnostic pipeline established in recent commits, ensuring consent status appears in `Mountain.dev.log` rather than the browser console.\n\nBoth changes ensure that `Output` polyfill artifacts rely on the Rust backend for diagnostics and do not pollute the runtime console with expected behavior errors.",
			"SHA": "50dd492ca0b69e13a675a9931a7ee21fdd3ea6ed"
		}
